  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q15",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Let the roots of $x^2-3x+10=0$ be $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$.\nFind the equation of the quadratic with roots $\\alpha+2$ and $\\beta+2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^2-7x+20=0$.",
      "worked": "$\\alpha+\\beta=3$, $\\alpha\\beta=10$.\n\nLet the new quadratic be $x^2+\\frac{b}{a}x+\\frac{c}{a}=0$.\n\nSum of roots:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha+2)+(\\beta+2)&=-\\frac{b}{a}\\\\\\alpha+\\beta+4&=-\\frac{b}{a}\\\\7&=-\\frac{b}{a}\\end{aligned}$$\nProduct of roots:\n$$\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha+2)(\\beta+2)&=\\frac{c}{a}\\\\\\alpha\\beta+2(\\alpha+\\beta)+4&=\\frac{c}{a}\\\\10+2(3)+4&=\\frac{c}{a}\\\\20&=\\frac{c}{a}\\end{aligned}$$\nTherefore $x^2-7x+20=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 56
  },
